  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Why",
    body:
        "When both hands alternate, one can hide behind the other. Alone, each hand has to keep time, keep its height and keep relaxed by itself. On the kit one hand often plays the hi-hat or ride for minutes while the other does something else: this is where that stamina starts.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "How",
    body:
        "Play from the wrist, stick about 10 cm high, and let every stroke rebound before the next one. Faster notes mean a smaller, quicker wrist motion, not a tighter grip. In the sixteenths of line 8 the fingers start helping: they close gently to play the note, and the rebound lifts the stick back up. The resting hand lies still on your leg.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Tips",
    body:
        "Count out loud, a single hand drifts in time more easily than two. Compare the left hand with the right: same sound, same height? If the forearm gets tight, stop, shake out, start again slower. Lines 5 and 7 use a gallop (eighth, two sixteenths): keep the eighth note long.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Song examples",
    body:
